'''''La Frontera, Balboa''''' is an inland [[comarca]] in [[Migjorn Province]], [[Balboa]]. It is situated in the southern interior of the province, between the more densely settled canal corridor comarcas to the north and the sparsely populated southern comarcas along the [[Sinchew]] border. The comarca had a population of 91,035 in 2026 and a total area of 1,226 km², giving it a population density of 74.2 inhabitants per square kilometre — moderate by Migjorn standards but above the provincial average for inland comarcas. The comarca capital is [[Sant Tomàs]].

The name ''La Frontera'' (Volisanian: "the frontier") reflects the comarca's historical position as a frontier zone during the colonial period, when the area marked the effective limit of Volisanian colonial control before the dense jungles and indigenous territories to the south. The name is shared with [[La Frontera (Balisca)|an unrelated historical frontier region]] in [[Balisca]].

== Geography ==

La Frontera is an entirely inland comarca, with no coastline on either the Shendan Ocean or the Aethiopian Ocean. It is bordered by [[La Garrotxa (comarca)|La Garrotxa]] to the north, [[L'Oliverar (comarca)|L'Oliverar]] to the east, and [[Cap del Sud (comarca)|Cap del Sud]] to the south. The terrain consists of rolling hills and dissected plateaus characteristic of Migjorn's interior, with elevations generally between 100 and 300 metres. Several small streams drain southward and westward through the comarca, forming tributaries of the broader river systems of southern Migjorn.

The comarca lies on the transitional zone between the fertile agricultural plains of the canal corridor and the more rugged, forested terrain of the southern border region. The northern portion of the comarca is more densely settled and cultivated, while the southern portion retains larger areas of forest and pasture.

=== Climate ===

La Frontera has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} ({{w|Köppen climate classification|Köppen}} Am), with average daily highs of 30 to 32 °C and lows of 22 to 24 °C. The wet season extends from May to November, with annual precipitation averaging approximately 2,000 to 2,400 mm. The inland position of the comarca results in slightly lower rainfall than the coastal comarcas, but the surrounding hills can produce localised orographic rainfall during the wet season.

== Demographics ==

La Frontera had a population of 91,035 in 2026, of which approximately 87,716 resided in the comarca capital, [[Sant Tomàs]]. The population is predominantly [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboan]], descended from enslaved workers brought to the colonial plantations of southern Migjorn. A smaller [[Fosian (Balboa)|Fosian]] community is present, primarily in Sant Tomàs, descended from Sinchewese workers who settled in the area during the Zong Balboa period. The [[White Balboan people|White Balboan]] population is small and concentrated in the comarca's administrative and commercial centre.

== Economy ==

The economy of La Frontera is primarily agricultural, with the northern portion of the comarca under cultivation for sugar cane, maize, and tropical fruits. The southern portion supports cattle ranching and timber extraction. Sant Tomàs functions as a local market and service centre for the surrounding agricultural area, with small-scale food processing, agricultural supply businesses, and retail trade.

The comarca's position along the secondary road network connecting the canal corridor to the southern comarcas provides some economic activity from transport and waystation services, though the comarca is not on any of the principal expressway corridors.

== Transport ==

La Frontera is connected to the provincial transport network by secondary roads linking Sant Tomàs to the [[Expressway 1 (Balboa)|E1]] corridor to the east and to the [[Expressway 6 (Balboa)|E6]] east–west route. The comarca is not served by the [[Canal Line (Balboa)|Canal Line]] railway, which runs through the canal corridor to the north. Local bus services connect Sant Tomàs to neighbouring comarca capitals.

== History ==

During the Volisanian colonial period, the area that now constitutes La Frontera comarca marked the effective southern limit of colonial agricultural settlement in Migjorn. The land beyond — corresponding to the modern comarcas of Cap del Sud and L'Aldea — remained largely outside colonial control, inhabited by indigenous communities and accessible only through difficult jungle terrain. The comarca's name preserves this historical role as the colonial frontier.

The colonial administration established Sant Tomàs as a small administrative and military outpost to secure the southern boundary of the plantation zone. The settlement grew slowly, supported by the surrounding sugar and cacao plantations that expanded into the comarca's northern hills during the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.

Following the [[Second War of the Isthmus]] (1893–1899) and the establishment of [[Zong Balboa]], La Frontera became part of the rump Balboan territory south of the Zong-controlled canal zone. The comarca's relative isolation from the northern provinces increased during this period, as the canal zone severed the overland connection to the rest of Balboa. The agricultural economy contracted, and infrastructure investment was minimal.

The [[Adonian Community]] mandate (1950–1960) and the [[Treaty of Balboa Harbour]] (1960) reunited Migjorn with the rest of Balboa, restoring the overland connection. Post-reunification investment in the provincial road network gradually improved La Frontera's accessibility, though the comarca remained less developed than the canal corridor comarcas.

